  - OEIS A084945
abstract: >-
  Rigorous interval-arithmetic certificate for the first 50,000 decimal
  digits of the Golomb-Dickman constant
  lambda = integral_0^infinity exp(-u - E_1(u)) du. The certificate gives
  integers Lambda_- < Lambda_+ and a scale S = 166293 such that
  lambda lies in [Lambda_-/2^S, Lambda_+/2^S] and
  floor(10^50000 Lambda_-/2^S) = floor(10^50000 Lambda_+/2^S); the digits
  are therefore proved by truncation. The interval width is
  4.390 x 10^-50043, leaving 42 guard digits. The package also contains
  the producing code and checkpoints, and an OEIS b-file for A084945 with
  terms n = 0..49999. The previous 40,000-digit certificate is kept in
  the same repository under 40000/.
